 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 953,
   "end": 2405,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "This is interpres."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 2561,
   "end": 6258,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "MCP servers are how AI",
    "apps reach tools and data,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 6258,
   "end": 7945,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "and thousands of them are public."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 7945,
   "end": 11626,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "interpres connects them to",
    "AssemblyAI's Voice Agent API."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 11626,
   "end": 16068,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Type a website, press the mic,",
    "and its tools answer out loud."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 17463,
   "end": 24769,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "AssemblyAI lists its Voice Agent API at",
    "$4.50 an hour, and OpenAI Realtime at $18."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 25003,
   "end": 27993,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Realtime can call MCP servers by itself."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 28115,
   "end": 31098,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "The Voice Agent API has no MCP tool type,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 31098,
   "end": 34627,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "so teams that move over for",
    "the price lose their MCP tools."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 34627,
   "end": 36270,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "interpres gives them back."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 38101,
   "end": 40542,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Here's a real website with an MCP server."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 40542,
   "end": 44907,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "interpres looks in the official",
    "MCP registry, finds the server,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 44907,
   "end": 48385,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "and turns each of its tools into",
    "a Voice Agent function tool."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 51108,
   "end": 53758,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Agent: Connected to Goji,",
    "with 9 tools available."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 53758,
   "end": 55145,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "What would you like to do?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 55936,
   "end": 58222,
   "who": "caller",
   "lines": [
    "Caller: What is SEO in plain English?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 62101,
   "end": 64620,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Agent: SEO, or search engine optimization,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 64620,
   "end": 66331,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "is the work of making",
    "your website the result"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 66331,
   "end": 68011,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "that search engines choose to show."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 68011,
   "end": 71418,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "This involves creating content that",
    "answers what people are searching for,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 71418,
   "end": 73771,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "ensuring your site is",
    "easy for engines to read,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 73771,
   "end": 76532,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "and building a reputation",
    "that other sites confirm…"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 77846,
   "end": 81730,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "That answer came from goji's own server,",
    "through a live tool call."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 82839,
   "end": 84646,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "No website in mind?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 84690,
   "end": 88877,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Search more than 11,000 public",
    "MCP servers right on the page."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 88877,
   "end": 90411,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "One click connects."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 92051,
   "end": 93791,
   "who": "caller",
   "lines": [
    "Caller: Who recommends Sapiens?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 98135,
   "end": 101360,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Agent: Sapiens is recommended",
    "by 32 verified people,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 101360,
   "end": 103902,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "including Joe Rogan and Lex Fridman."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 105018,
   "end": 107592,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Many servers list more than ten tools."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 107666,
   "end": 112064,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "interpres shows the agent ten at a time,",
    "and one of them is find tools."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 112064,
   "end": 113830,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Ask for something out of view:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 113830,
   "end": 117222,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "interpres swaps the right",
    "tools in, mid-conversation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 118795,
   "end": 121579,
   "who": "caller",
   "lines": [
    "Caller: I want to run a spec",
    "check on a job contract."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 123837,
   "end": 125539,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Agent: I can certainly help with that."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 125539,
   "end": 128612,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Please provide the job contract",
    "you would like me to check."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 130580,
   "end": 134235,
   "who": "caller",
   "lines": [
    "Caller: What is the reputation",
    "of wallet 0x5A AEB6…"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 134235,
   "end": 137014,
   "who": "caller",
   "lines": [
    "…1BEA ED?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 142462,
   "end": 144084,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Agent: I may have misheard that value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 144084,
   "end": 146813,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Please paste it into the",
    "box under the talk button,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 146813,
   "end": 149035,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "and I will use exactly what you paste."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 150953,
   "end": 155161,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "A spoken address is held back,",
    "right or wrong. Nothing runs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 155926,
   "end": 158259,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Speech often mishears identifiers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 158413,
   "end": 162665,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Before this gate, a misheard wallet",
    "address reached the server 5 times,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 162665,
   "end": 165399,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "and a right hearing looks",
    "exactly like a wrong one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 165489,
   "end": 169539,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "So the address comes from the paste box,",
    "and the agent uses the exact text."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 171364,
   "end": 173971,
   "who": "caller",
   "lines": [
    "Caller: Check the reputation",
    "of the wallet I pasted."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 179311,
   "end": 181656,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "Agent: That wallet has no",
    "recorded job outcomes yet,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 181656,
   "end": 183990,
   "who": "agent",
   "lines": [
    "either as a provider or as a buyer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 184944,
   "end": 186388,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "To check it isn't just these three,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 186388,
   "end": 190327,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "we probed every remote server",
    "in the official MCP registry."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 190401,
   "end": 192969,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "12,012 answered without a login,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 192969,
   "end": 197148,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "listing more than 200,000 tools,",
    "and every tool converted."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 198588,
   "end": 202439,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Then we gave thirty of them one",
    "spoken question each, untuned."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 202439,
   "end": 206065,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Twenty-nine sessions ran,",
    "each one answered out loud,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 206065,
   "end": 208430,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "and fourteen answered from live data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 208617,
   "end": 213030,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "When a tool ran, the median",
    "was 3.5 seconds voice to voice,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 213030,
   "end": 215330,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "and the whole run cost 60 cents."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 216756,
   "end": 221185,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Along the way we found two places where",
    "the API behaves differently from its docs,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 221185,
   "end": 223959,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "and wrote both up with",
    "scripts that reproduce them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 225304,
   "end": 226643,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Who is it for?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 226815,
   "end": 230125,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Teams leaving OpenAI Realtime",
    "add the library to their agent"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 230125,
   "end": 233747,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "and keep every MCP server it calls,",
    "at a quarter of the price."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 233822,
   "end": 238456,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Any public MCP server gets a voice",
    "interface, with no change on its side."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 238547,
   "end": 240834,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "The library ships in the same repo."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 241713,
   "end": 246725,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "interpres is open source under MIT,",
    "and live now at the address on screen."
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 246786,
   "end": 249495,
   "who": "narration",
   "lines": [
    "Type a website, press the mic, and ask."
   ]
  }
 ],
